  "conclusion": "One stable global rank-480 atlas contains about 72% of the dense teacher input-Jacobian row energy, and unrestricted node-specific coefficients reproduce 92-98% of sampled preactivation energy and more than 91.6% of routed output. Nevertheless their self-consistent GELU tangent recovers only 19.6-21.5% of dense input JVP, including the heldout-leaking arm. The rank and cross-bank atlas identification are not the primary failure; unweighted preactivation regression does not preserve activation-boundary motion. The registered ridge realization is closed, and the compact pseudo-random map cannot yet be named the sole bottleneck.",
